// error
// E0047 catches a struct cycle of ANY length, not just the one-hop self-edge
// (#1923). Before this, `struct S { s: S }` was rejected while the identical
// two-struct spelling was accepted and ran.
//
// A struct field is one 8-byte handle, so the LAYOUT of a cycle is finite —
// that is why the check looked stale. But layout was never the binding
// constraint. A struct has no nil (SPEC §13.4), so a struct-typed field can
// neither be omitted (E0083) nor filled with nothing, and filling one obliges
// filling one more:
//
//     A{ b: B{ a: A{ b: B{ a: ...     // no base case, ever
//
// So the cycle is uninstantiable at every length and belongs at the
// declaration, where one error names it, rather than at each construction site
// as a separate E0083.
//
// Each cycle is reported ONCE, from whichever member is reached first, not once
// per member — a three-struct cycle is one defect. The caret sits on the edge
// that closes the cycle, which is the edge to change.
//
// run_struct_cycle_option.bit pins the escape hatch this hint names.
struct A { b: B }
struct B { a: A }

struct P { q: Q }
struct Q { r: R }
struct R { p: P }
